    "show_share": true,
    "description": "In developing countries such as Pakistan, diarrhoea continues to be a major killer of children during the first five years of life. A seminar organised at Aga Khan University (AKU) in collaboration with University of Maryland (USA) highlighted the role of systematic medical research and the development of new vaccines to tackle the huge burden of diarrhoea-related deaths. Dr Myron M. Levine, Director of the internationally renowned Centre for Vaccine Development at the University of Maryland, and Dr Anita Zaidi, Associate Professor of Paediatrics and Child Health at AKU were the invited speakers at this seminar.",
